# Common Layer (all platforms)

Shared code lives at **`lib/` root** (conceptually the “common” layer). **Never** put platform-specific widgets or layouts here.

## Folders

| Path | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `lib/config/` | API base URL, env, host resolution |
| `lib/design/` | Brand tokens, theme, shared typography (`app_tokens.dart`) |
| `lib/l10n/` | ARB files + generated localizations |
| `lib/models/` | DTOs / domain models |
| `lib/providers/` | Riverpod — API, session, catalog, downloads |
| `lib/router/` | `go_router` routes and navigation helpers |
| `lib/storage/` | Secure storage, caches, prefs |
| `lib/utils/` | Pure helpers (no `BuildContext`, no platform UI) |
| `lib/common/platform/` | Shell guards: `useMobileShell`, `useWebShell`, `useDesktopShell` |
| `lib/screens/` | **Route adapters only** — wire providers, branch to platform UI |

## Rules

- One implementation per feature for data, auth, sync, and business rules.
- Import **down** into platform folders; platform folders must **not** export upward into common.
- Common may import Flutter core only — not `lib/mobile/`, `lib/web/`, or `lib/desktop/`.
- All user-visible strings in `lib/l10n/` — no hardcoded copy in common or platform code.
- Shared brand: `AppColors`, `AppSpace`, `AppRadius`, `AppTheme`. Platform folders may add **extensions** (`WebTokens`, `MobileTokens`, `DesktopTokens`) that reference shared tokens.

## Route adapter pattern (`lib/screens/`)

Screen files orchestrate; they do **not** own platform layout trees:

```dart
// lib/screens/home_screen.dart
if (useWebShell(context)) {
  return const WebPageScaffold(body: HomeScreenBody());
}
if (useDesktopShell(context)) {
  return const DesktopPageScaffold(body: HomeScreenBody());
}
return const MobileHomeScreen(); // lib/mobile/screens/
```
